#question(title: [Composition of one-to-one functions -- 2])[
  Assume for simplicity that all functions in
  this problem have domain $RR$. Prove the
  following theorem.

  #slide-block(title: [Theorem B])[
    Let $f$ and $g$ be functions.  \
    IF $f circle.small g$ is one-to-one,
    #h(1em) THEN $g$ is one-to-one.
  ]

  Suggestion:
  + Transform the “$display(P ==> Q)$”
    theorem into an equivalent
    #box[“$display("(not Q)" ==> "(not P)")$”]
    theorem.  \
     You will prove that one instead.
  + Write the definition of the hypotheses  \
     and of the conclusion.
  + Write the proof.
]
